Source code of the third-party parts in this package (schneidi @VERSION@)
=======================================================================

This package contains programs and libraries under the GNU General Public License (GPL-2.0-or-later: FFmpeg as
built here with x264 and x265, x264, x265) and the GNU Lesser General Public License (LGPL: FFmpeg's libraries, Qt,
libnuma and others listed in THIRD_PARTY.md). Their licences let you get, change and share the complete source code
of these parts.

Where the source is
-------------------
The complete corresponding source code of these parts, for exactly this version, is published next to the package:

    https://github.com/OnkelTheorie/schneidi/releases/tag/v@VERSION@
    asset "schneidi-@VERSION@-gpl-sources.tar"

It contains the FFmpeg source release, the scripts and settings it was built with (packaging/linux/build-ffmpeg-lgpl.sh,
packaging/ffmpeg-components.txt), and the source packages of x264, x265 and libnuma that the binaries were built from
(Debian source packages for Linux and Docker, MSYS2 source packages for Windows). schneidi's own source code
(AGPL-3.0-only) is the repository itself: https://github.com/OnkelTheorie/schneidi (tag v@VERSION@).

Written offer
-------------
For at least three years after this version was released, anyone who received this package may ask for the complete
corresponding source code of its GPL and LGPL parts, on a medium customarily used for software interchange, for no
more than the cost of physically performing the source distribution. Ask by opening an issue at

    https://github.com/OnkelTheorie/schneidi/issues

and name the version (@VERSION@) and the package (AppImage, Windows or Docker image).
